==Russian==
{{wikipedia|lang=ru}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=ru|[nʌ'ga]}}
* {{audio|Ru-нога.ogg|Audio}}

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Slavic|noga|lang=ru}}, < Proto-Indo-European ''*(o)nogʰ-'' ‘claw, nail’. Cognate with English ''[[nail]]'', Latvian ''[[nagas]]'', Latin ''[[unguis]]'', Spanish ''[[uña]]'', Welsh ''[[ewin]]''.

===Noun===
{{infl|ru|noun|tr=nogá|g=f}}

# [[leg]]
# [[foot]]

====Usage notes====
Pronunciation of the genitive plural [[ног]] as “нох” is considered old-fashioned.

